\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Souls of men, why will ye scatter
\par Like a crowd of frightened sheep?
\par Foolish hearts, why will ye wander?
\par From a love so true and deep?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Was there ever kindest shepherd
\par Half so  gentle, half so sweet,
\par As the Saviour who would have us
\par Come and gather round His feet?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There's a wideness in God's mercy
\par Like the wideness of the sea;
\par There's a kindness in His justice
\par Which is more than liberty.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There is welcome for the sinner,
\par And more graces for the good;
\par There is mercy with the Saviour;
\par There is healing in His blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. There is plentiful redemption
\par In the blood that has been shed;
\par There is joy for all the members
\par In the sorrows of the Head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. For the love of God is broader
\par Than the measures of man's mind,
\par And the heart of the Eternal
\par Is most wonderfully kind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. If our love were but more simple,
\par We should take Him at His word,
\par And our lives would be all sunshine
\par In the sweetness of our Lord.\f1 
\par 
\par }

